From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: widen license-files to cover vendored expat/udunits2

Every platform's wheel (not just riscv64) statically links expat 2.6.0 and
UDUNITS-2 2.2.28 from the vendored extern/ sources, but license-files names
only gimli.units' own LICENSE.md, so neither dependency's notice travels
with the binary even though both require it.

Naming the two vendored notices alongside LICENSE.md lets the wheel build
stage them and have them land in .dist-info/licenses/.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [affects every platform's wheel, not a riscv64-only build detail]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 requires-python = ">=3.11"
 description = "An object-oriented Python interface to udunits"
 license = "MIT"
-license-files = ["LICENSE.md"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE.md", "extern/expat-2.6.0/COPYING", "extern/udunits-2.2.28/COPYRIGHT"]
 keywords = [
     "earth science",
     "model coupling",
